Package: endogCopulaBayes
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Gaussian Copula Endogeneity Correction
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Ashwin", family = "Malshe", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "ashwin@malshe.com")
Description: Implements the Bayesian 'Gaussian copula' endogeneity correction
    of Haschka (2026) <doi:10.1111/obes.70023> via a Metropolis-within-Gibbs
    sampler, ported from the published replication code into a standalone
    package. The sampler jointly estimates the regression coefficients, the
    residual variance, the copula correlation matrix, and Dirichlet
    probability masses describing the marginal distributions of the
    regressors, and returns the full MCMC chain alongside a thinned posterior
    sample with print and summary methods.
